   "text": "I read the drawing as a cyclic undecapeptide-like macrocycle carrying a linear side chain. The stereo-assignments for the top side chain and several ring residues came from the wedges and hashes; for the rest I assumed natural (L) configuration, so those are less certain.\n\n**Side chain (top, from the piperidine end):**\n- Piperidine amide, then L-Ala (H wedged, assigned S), then N\u2013H.\n- Next come N-Me-Phe and a second N-Me-Phe, each with a CH2Ph group.\n- The second N-Me-Phe is acylated onto the ring \u03b1-carbon.\n\n**Ring \u03b1-carbon:**\n- This is an Asp-type residue whose \u03b2-carbonyl is part of the ring.\n- Its \u03b1-carbon carries the exocyclic C(=O)N(Me) group, the ring NH and the ring CH2.\n\n**Ring sequence (from the Asp CH2, going around):**\n- CH2\u2013C(=O)\u2013N(Me)Ala\n- N(Me)Phe\n- N(Me)Leu\n- Thr (NH, with CH(OH)CH3)\n- N(Me)Ala\n- Val (NH, with isopropyl)\n- N(Me)Ala\n- N(Me)Ala\n- back to the NH of the Asp-type \u03b1-carbon\n\n**Stereochemistry:**\n- The wedges and hashes at Ala, Phe, Asp, Leu and Thr (C\u03b1 and the hydroxyl-bearing C\u03b2) give L-amino-acid configurations, with Thr as (2S,3R).\n- The remaining ring Ala and Val centres are too ambiguous to read, so I assigned them L.\n\nI checked the SMILES for ring-closure digits and atom counts against this trace.\n\nSMILES: O=C(N1CCCCC1)[C@H](C)NC(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)N(C)C(=O)[C@H](Cc1ccccc1)N(C)C(=O)[C@@H]1CC(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](Cc2ccccc2)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](CC(C)C)C(=O)N[C@@H]([C@@H](C)O)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N[C@@H](C(C)C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N(C)[C@@H](C)C(=O)N1"
